title:    How the implementation is organised
subtitle: Major directories only. Full source on GitHub.
width:    820
---
week-13-hybrid-connectivity/
├── LAB.md                      reproduction guide: ASNs, the /30s, teardown
├── terraform/
│   ├── main.tf                 gateways, routers, tunnels, BGP, probes
│   └── variables.tf            ASNs and the branch CIDR, with why each matters
├── scripts/
│   ├── measure-failover.py     the load-bearing measurement; restores in a trap
│   ├── gen-psk.sh              random IKE pre-shared key into gitignored tfvars
│   └── validate.sh             every assertion against the cloud, not state
└── docs/                       figure plan, references, screenshots

# terraform/  two VPCs, two gateways, two routers, four tunnels. The second
#             VPC stands in for a remote site - the protocols do not care
#             whether the peer is a VPC, on-prem hardware or another cloud.
# scripts/    measure-failover.py disables a BGP peer, so it re-enables it on
#             every path out including the failure path.
